                            <comment id="14548470" author="rnowling" created="Mon, 18 May 2015 18:30:54 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;The patch fixes most of our issues with PySpark and indentation.  The following test still fails:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;%pyspark
count = 0
&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; data.map(lambda x: x) \
        .collect():
    count += 1
print count
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In particular, Zeppelin does not account for statements over multiple lines (using \ ).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Do you want me to open a new JIRA for this?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14549425" author="moon" created="Mon, 18 May 2015 22:46:32 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Yes, please create an new issue&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
